+// neoxify-patch: ios-udp-flows. Every UDP source port the phone uses is a
+// flow here, and upstream keeps one until its outbound gives up on it --
+// 300 s idle for a proxied flow, 30-90 s for a refused one -- each with a
+// 1024-packet queue and its goroutines. A phone sends every lookup from a
+// new port, three per name, and QUIC attempts from new ports too, so
+// opening apps held thousands of flows inside an iOS packet tunnel that is
+// killed at about 50 MB (measured 2026-11-17: 49.2 MiB 30 s into a
+// session). Bounded here by design:
+//   - a shorter queue per flow (udpFlowQueue): room for a video call's
+//     burst on a slow TCP-carried transport, not for a backlog;
+//   - a flow ended when idle -- no packet either way -- for udpFlowIdle
+//     once it has had a reply (two minutes: calls on hold, peer-to-peer
+//     games and long keep-alives rely on that floor, and a flow ended
+//     early gets a new server-side port, so the far end's packets after a
+//     silence are lost), udpUnrepliedIdle while it has had none (a
+//     QUIC attempt nothing answers); for one to port 53, which is over in
+//     one reply, udpLookupIdle until it is answered (the slowest lookup
+//     takes 6 s) and udpAnsweredIdle after;
+//   - at most udpFlowMax flows at once and udpLookupMax lookups beside
+//     them, so a flood of one kind cannot starve the other; a packet that
+//     would open one more is dropped, as a full queue drops one. A phone
+//     has a handful of live UDP flows (calls, games, QUIC to a few hosts);
+//     on a protocol that carries each one in a connection of its own
+//     (Trojan, VLESS over WebSocket) a flow costs about 60 KiB, so 64 of
+//     them is about 4 MiB, and a QUIC attempt turned away falls back to
+//     TCP as it does wherever QUIC is blocked.
+const (
+	udpFlowQueue     = 256
+	udpFlowIdle      = 120 * time.Second
+	udpUnrepliedIdle = 15 * time.Second
+	udpLookupIdle    = 10 * time.Second
+	udpAnsweredIdle  = 2 * time.Second
+	udpFlowSweep     = time.Second
+	udpFlowMax       = 64
+	udpLookupMax     = 512
+)
+
